# Review requests for CI and agent configuration.
#
# These entries auto-request a review on the paths that decide what automation
# does: workflows and composite actions, the Copilot- and Claude-side
# instructions/skills/agents, and the devcontainer (whose `initializeCommand`
# runs on a developer's own machine).
#
# This file is deliberately ADVISORY. Do not enable "Require review from Code
# Owners" in branch protection: with a single owner it would block that owner's
# own pull requests, because an author never satisfies their own code-owner
# review. Adding a second owner just to unblock that makes them a bottleneck on
# every CI change.
#
# What actually gates these paths is .github/workflows/guard-agent-config.yml,
# which fails when an AGENT-authored pull request touches them until a human
# adds the `agent-config-approved` label. That distinguishes "a person changed
# CI" from "an agent changed CI" - which is the real concern - without making
# anyone wait on a second reviewer.

/.github/       @rajbos
/.claude/       @rajbos
/AGENTS.md      @rajbos
/CLAUDE.md      @rajbos
/.devcontainer/ @rajbos
